# Demo Data

Owns curated + volume demo seeding for local/demo environments. Never seed production.

## Workflow

- Commands: `db:clear:demo` → `db:seed:demo` → `db:verify:demo` (or `db:reset:demo`).
- Orchestrator: `seed-demo-data.js` with P012 pack order, then `seed-volume-pack`, then `seed-volume-extended-pack`, then optional filler when volume is skipped.
- Gate all clear/seed work with `demo-safety.js` (refuse production / live DB URLs).

## Volume

- `SEED_RECORD_COUNT` defaults to **1000**; `0` is curated-only.
- Core volume tables must reach the target: patients, appointments, encounters, admissions, lab/pharmacy/radiology, invoices/payments, emergencies, stock movements, biomed work orders, mortuary cases, notifications.
- Extended volume (lived-in facility): diagnoses, vitals, procedures, nursing notes/ward rounds/MAR/discharges, visit queues, refunds/adjustments/insurance claims/pre-auths/enrollments, triage/ambulance trips, shifts/payroll, audit/PHI logs, report definitions/runs/schedules, KPIs, analytics events, patient report jobs, messages, clinical notes/care plans/alerts/allergies, theatre cases, beds/assignments, imaging studies, referrals/follow-ups, price books/scheme offers.
- Exclude intentional singletons/catalogs: one demo tenant/facility/subscription/license; plan/add-on/module catalogs; role/permission catalogs; `_prisma_migrations`.

## Scenario Coverage

- Keep curated hero scenarios asserted by `verify-demo-data` (roles/emails, subscription health, communications variants, biomedical/compliance baselines, break-glass pending + **ACTIVE** approved).
- Accountant demo (`accountant@hosspi.com`) must resolve Accounts desk access when `facility-accounts` is entitled; HR demo users must not gain `accounts:*` from the HR role pack alone.
- Volume rows must diversify statuses so demo role logins see non-empty, filterable queues (including Accounts open work / to-post / approvals when Accounts packs seed).
- Prefer FK-valid related graphs and deterministic upserts (`deterministicUuid` / pack keys). Do not invent orphan foreign keys.

## Safety And Verify

- Break-glass ACTIVE rows must use real-world-future `expires_at` so expiry sweeps do not flip them before verify.
- Verify raises volume floors when `SEED_RECORD_COUNT > 0`; curated invariants always apply.
- Seed remains deterministic for a fixed `SEED_RANDOM_SEED`.

